OAuth Pentest Checklist (Bug Bounty / Pentest)

1. Identify OAuth Flow
Check for social login options (Google, GitHub, etc.)
Identify the Authorization endpoint (e.g., /authorize)
Identify the Token endpoint (e.g., /token)
Determine the OAuth grant type:
Authorization Code
Implicit
Hybrid
Device / PKCE
Verify whether PKCE is implemented (especially for SPA / Mobile)

2. redirect_uri Validation (Critical)
Check if redirect_uri uses exact matching or wildcard
Test subdomain manipulation:
https://evil.client.com
Test open redirect via redirect_uri parameter:
redirect_uri=https://client.com/redirect?next=https://evil.com
Test URL encoding / double encoding
Test fragment injection (#)
Test trailing slash / case sensitivity
Test HTTP → HTTPS downgrade
Impact: Token leakage, account takeover

3. state Parameter (OAuth CSRF)
Verify presence of state
Remove the state parameter completely
Modify the state value
Verify correlation between request and callback
Check whether state is random and non-predictable
Impact: Login CSRF, account linking attack

4. Response Type Abuse
Test switching response_type=code ↔ response_type=token
Test invalid combinations, e.g.:
response_type=code token
Check if the authorization server allows implicit flow for web applications
Impact: Token exposure / token leakage

5. Authorization Code Tests
Attempt to reuse the authorization code
Attempt to exchange the code with:
a different client_id
a different redirect_uri
Check if the code has proper expiration
Test using the same code across multiple sessions
Impact: Full account takeover
6. Token Security (Access / ID Token)

Check for token leakage in:
URL
Referer header
localStorage
server logs
Verify JWT security:
alg=none
signature validation
aud, iss, exp
Check if tokens are properly bound to the user and client
Impact: Session hijacking

7. Scope Manipulation
Try adding extra scopes:
scope=openid profile email admin
Remove required scopes
Check if scopes can be granted without user approval
Impact: Privilege escalation

8. Client Validation
Verify binding between client_id and redirect_uri
Test using another application's client_id
Check that client_secret is not exposed in the frontend
Impact: Token misbinding

9. PKCE (if implemented)
Remove code_verifier
Modify code_verifier
Check for S256 vs plain enforcement
Verify that PKCE is enforced when required
Impact: Authorization code interception

10. Account Linking / Social Login
Login without verifying email ownership
Link attacker’s OAuth account to victim’s account
Change identity provider during callback
Verify email ownership checks
Impact: Account takeover

11. Logout & Session Handling
Verify token validity after logout
Check for token revocation endpoint
Test for session fixation



Top Bug Bounty Targets (Priority)

redirect_uri validation
state parameter protection
Authorization code reuse
Token leakage
Account linking / social login issues
